Subject: [PATCH 1/2] =?UTF-8?q?feat(blueprints):=20BP-57=20/=20Q27-A3=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20a=20local=20survives=20a=20suspension?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A suspension is `return NodeStatus.Running`: the C# frame dies and a stack
local with it, so a value written before a Delay read back as its DEFAULT
after the resume — clean compile, no diagnostic, wrong number.

Q27-A3: a graph that can suspend gets a graph-scoped blackboard slot instead,
reset in the ENTRY block rather than at the top of the method. The entry block
is reached only when `__phase == 0`, and the phase is cleared before control
reaches the resume block, so the reset fires once per INVOCATION and survives
every suspension inside it. "Per-invocation" was never "per-frame" — A1
conflated them because in a non-suspending graph they coincide. A graph that
cannot suspend keeps today's plain C# local, untouched.

The slots live in their own IrAsset list, never appended to
Variables/WorkingState/Parameters: those three are a positional index space
FindVariableIndex and VarFieldName already disagree about (BP-226), and a
fourth source would make that ambiguity live. Slots are addressed by name
only. They DO enter StructureHash — they occupy real blackboard bytes, and
the emitted BTreeTick re-initialises that memory only on a hash mismatch, so
a slot outside the hash would let a changed type reinterpret stale bytes.

Also closes a six-batch gap the storage choice depends on: MacroLatency.IsLatent
listed three node kinds and omitted ChannelCommandNode with ActionFqn set, which
Stage5.ScheduleInlineActionNode turns into IrOp_InlineActionCall and the wait
lowering splits into a suspend/resume state machine. BP1661 and collapse
legality both read such a macro as synchronous. The node-level and op-level
predicates are now one list each with a test asserting they agree.

